      "origin": [2, 5],
      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Dolores Varga ran Suds & Spin for twenty-two years and let the three flats over it. When the Cordon shut the valley she kept the machines turning for anyone with quarters until the water pressure went, then chained the front doors, locked the back stair at the bottom and kept its key on the board in her change office. Upstairs the Bauers nailed their own door shut and lived on what Anja had stocked; next door Hal Ostrowski coughed through the wall for a week and then went quiet. On the ninth night he came through it, the plaster and the lath, with his hands. Tom Bauer held the hole with a fire axe while Anja took their boy out of the bathroom window onto the sign and down. Tom is still in the front room. Somebody crawled into the big dryer at the end of the row and never came out, and the pickup that went through the side wall is how everyone has come in since.",
